    "_meanings": [
        ".²1\n",
        ".³({%a%}) Power, ability, capacity, strength, energy, prowess; {#dEvaM#}\n {#nihatya kuru pOruzamAtmaSaktyA#} <ls>Pt. 1. 361</ls>; {#jYAne mOnaM kzamA SaktO#}\n <ls>R. 1. 22</ls>; so {#yaTASakti, svaSakti#} <ab>&c.</ab>\n",
        ".³({%b%}) Faculty, capacity; {#smaraRaSakti#} ‘retentive faculty or memory’.\n",
        ".²2 Regal power; (it has three parts or elements; 1 {#praBuSakti#} or {#praBAvaSakti#}\n ‘the majesty or pre-eminent position of the king himself’; 2 {#maMtraSakti#}\n ‘the power of good counsel’; and 3 {#utsAhaSakti#} ‘the power of energy’);\n {#rAjyaM nAma SaktitrayAyattam#} <ls>Dk.</ls>; {#trisADanA SaktirivArTasaMcayam#}\n <ls>R. 3. 13</ls>, <ls n=\"R.\">6. 33</ls>, <ls n=\"R.\">17. 63</ls>; <ls>Śi. 2. 26</ls>.\n",
        ".²3 The power of composition, poetic power or genius; {#SaktirnipuRatA#}\n {#lokaSAstrakAvyAdyavekzaRAt#} <ls>K. P. 1</ls>; see explanation {%ad loc.%}\n",
        ".²4 The active power of a deity, regarded as his wife, female divinity;\n (these are variously enumerated, 8, 9 or even 50 being mentioned); {#sa#}\n {#jayati pariRadDaH SaktiBiH SaktinATaH#} <ls>Māl. 5. 1</ls>; <ls>Ś. 7. 35</ls>.\n",
        ".²5 A kind of missile; {#SaktiKaRqAmarzitena gARqIvinoktam#} <ls>Ve. 3</ls>; {#tato#}\n {#biBeda pOlastyaH SaktyA vakzasi lakzmaRam#} <ls>R. 12. 77</ls>.\n",
        ".²6 A spear, dart, pike, lance.\n",
        ".²7 (In <ab>phil.</ab>) The relation of a term to the thing designated.\n",
        ".²8 The power inherent in cause to produce its necessary effect.\n",
        ".²9 (In <ab>Rhet.</ab>) The power or signification of a word; (these are three {#aBiDA#},\n {#lakzaRA#} and {#vyaYjanA#}); {#tisraH Sabdasya SaktayaH#} <ls>S. D. 11</ls>.\n",
        ".²10 The expressive power or denotation of a word (<ab>opp.</ab> {#lakzaRA#} and\n {#vyaYjanA#}); it is thus defined:-- {#asmAcCabdAdayamarTo bodDavya ityAkArako'nAdisaMketaH#}\n {#SaktiH#} <ls>Tarka K.</ls>\n",
        ".²11 The female organ, the counterpart of the Phallus of Śiva worshipped\n by a sect of people called Śāktas.\n",
        ".²12 A sword.\n",
        ".²13 An implement in gambling.\n"
    ],
